        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Harfleur, August 1415",
      "narration": "In August 1415, Henry crossed the Channel with around ten to twelve thousand men, and laid siege to the port of Harfleur in Normandy.",
      "word_count": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-10",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Harfleur",
      "start": 169,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-10.png",
      "background": "siege",
      "camera": "shake",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "He expected the town to fall quickly. It held out for more than a month, while his cannons pounded the walls day after day.",
      "word_count": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-11",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Harfleur",
      "start": 180,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-11.png",
      "background": "siege",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Sick archer",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "sit"
        },
        {
          "name": "Sick archer",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "sit"
        },
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "But the real enemy was already inside his camp. A terrible disease called dysentery swept through the army. Thousands fell sick. Some were gone within days. Many more had to be sent home.",
      "word_count": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-12",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Harfleur",
      "start": 194,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-12.png",
      "background": "siege",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Harfleur finally surrendered in late September. Henry had his town. But he had lost a large part of his army, and winter was coming.",
      "word_count": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-13",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The long march",
      "start": 205,
      "duration": 21,
      "image": "images/shot-13.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Adviser",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Adviser",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "His advisers told him to go home by sea. Henry refused. Instead, he decided to march his remaining men overland to Calais, an English-held town on the coast. It was partly a show of strength: the King of England walking through France, and nobody able to stop him.",
      "word_count": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-14",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The long march",
      "start": 226,
      "duration": 6,
      "image": "images/shot-14.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Food for 8 days",
      "narration": "The men carried enough food for about eight days. That was the plan.",
      "word_count": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-15",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The long march",
      "start": 232,
      "duration": 8,
      "image": "images/shot-15.png",
      "background": "river",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "The River Somme",
      "narration": "Then they reached the River Somme. Every bridge and every crossing was broken or guarded by French troops.",
      "word_count": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-16",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The long march",
      "start": 240,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-16.png",
      "background": "river",
      "camera": "track left",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "So the English had to march inland, upstream, searching for a way across. Day after day, in the cold October rain. The eight days of food ran out. Men picked nuts and berries from the hedges to stay alive.",
      "word_count": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-17",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The long march",
      "start": 257,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-17.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "slow zoom out",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "It took them about two and a half weeks. And all the while, the French army was gathering behind the river, growing bigger every day.",
      "word_count": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-18",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The long march",
      "start": 268,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-18.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Agincourt, 24 October",
      "narration": "On the twenty-fourth of October, near a village called Agincourt, they finally saw them. The French army was right in front of them, blocking the road to Calais.",
      "word_count": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-19",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 280,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-19.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "bow"
        },
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "bow"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "That night, it poured. The English camped in the open: wet, cold and hungry. Henry ordered total silence in his camp. Many of his men expected not to see another sunset, and spent the night in prayer.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-20",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 296,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-20.png",
      "background": "camp",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "sit"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "sit"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "On the other side, according to some chroniclers, the French camp was noisy and confident. Some knights were said to be playing dice for the rich English prisoners they expected to capture the next day.",
      "word_count": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-21",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 311,
      "duration": 26,
      "image": "images/shot-21.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Outnumbered 3 or 4 to 1?",
      "narration": "How big were the armies? Henry had perhaps six to nine thousand men, and most of them, maybe five out of every six, were archers. The French are often said to have had three or four times as many. Some modern historians think the gap was smaller. But everyone agrees: the English were badly outnumbered, and in far worse shape.",
      "word_count": 60
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-22",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The longbow",
      "start": 337,
      "duration": 5,
      "image": "images/shot-22.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "The English longbow",
      "narration": "But those archers had a secret weapon. The English longbow.",
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-23",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The longbow",
      "start": 342,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-23.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Young archer",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Old archer",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "It was a simple stick of yew wood, almost as tall as a man. But pulling one took enormous strength. English boys trained from childhood, and by law, men were expected to practise archery on Sundays and holidays.",
      "word_count": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-24",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The longbow",
      "start": 359,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-24.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "10+ arrows a minute",
      "narration": "A good archer could shoot ten or more arrows a minute, at targets about two hundred and fifty yards away. Five thousand archers could send tens of thousands of arrows into the sky in a single minute.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-25",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The longbow",
      "start": 375,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-25.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Each archer also carried a long wooden stake, sharpened at both ends. Hammered into the ground at an angle, a row of them could stop a charging horse.",
      "word_count": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-26",
      "speaker": null,
