        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "The woods on both sides squeezed the field narrower. Whatever the French did, they couldn't spread out and surround Henry's small army. They would have to come straight at him.",
      "word_count": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-28",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The field",
      "start": 414,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-28.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "And then... nothing happened. For hours, the two armies just stood there, staring at each other. The French were happy to wait. Time was on their side. The English were the ones running out of food.",
      "word_count": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-29",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The field",
      "start": 430,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-29.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "track left",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "So Henry made a bold move. He ordered his whole army to pull up their stakes and walk forward, toward the enemy, until the French were within bow range. Then the archers hammered their stakes back into the mud.",
      "word_count": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-30",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The field",
      "start": 447,
      "duration": 3,
      "image": "images/shot-30.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "shake",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Loose!",
      "narration": "And the archers began to shoot.",
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-31",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Into the mud",
      "start": 450,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-31.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "shake",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "The arrows provoked the French into attacking. Their mounted knights charged at the edges of the English line. But the woods squeezed them together, the stakes stopped their horses, and the arrows kept coming.",
      "word_count": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-32",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Into the mud",
      "start": 465,
      "duration": 10,
      "image": "images/shot-32.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "track left",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Panicking horses turned and galloped back, straight into their own soldiers who were advancing on foot. The mud got churned up even worse.",
      "word_count": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-33",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Into the mud",
      "start": 475,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-33.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Now the main French army walked forward. Thousands of men in heavy steel armor, trudging through deep mud while arrows rained down on them. By the time they reached the English line, many of them were already exhausted.",
      "word_count": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-34",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Into the mud",
      "start": 492,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-34.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "shake",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Fallen knight",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "And the field kept narrowing. The French were packed so tightly that many couldn't even raise their weapons. Men who slipped in the mud struggled to get back up.",
      "word_count": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-35",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Into the mud",
      "start": 505,
      "duration": 18,
      "image": "images/shot-35.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "shake",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "walk"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Then the English archers dropped their bows, picked up swords, axes and the wooden mallets they'd used for the stakes, and ran into the fight. Lightly dressed, they could move easily through the mud. The knights could barely move at all.",
      "word_count": 41
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-36",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Into the mud",
      "start": 523,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-36.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Henry fought in the front line himself, with a crown on his helmet. One story says a French knight struck him so hard that part of the crown was knocked off.",
      "word_count": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-37",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The darkest moment",
      "start": 537,
      "duration": 24,
      "image": "images/shot-37.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Prisoner",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "bow"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Then came the darkest moment of the day. Fearing a fresh French attack, and worried that his many prisoners might join it, Henry ordered that most of them be struck down. Even his own men hesitated. It is still the most controversial decision of the battle, and historians argue about it to this day.",
      "word_count": 54
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-38",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The darkest moment",
      "start": 561,
      "duration": 6,
      "image": "images/shot-38.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "slow zoom out",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "The new attack never really came. By the afternoon, it was over.",
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-39",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The herald's answer",
      "start": 567,
      "duration": 20,
      "image": "images/shot-39.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Montjoie",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "After the battle, according to the chroniclers, Henry asked the French royal herald, Montjoie, who had won. The herald answered: the King of England. Henry asked the name of the castle nearby. Agincourt, came the reply. Then this, said Henry, shall be called the Battle of Agincourt.",
      "word_count": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-40",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The herald's answer",
      "start": 587,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-40.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "France: thousands lost · England: a few hundred",
      "narration": "The losses were completely one-sided. The French lost thousands of men, including a huge part of their nobility: dukes, counts, and the commander of the royal army himself. The English lost a few hundred at most.",
      "word_count": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-41",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Why it worked",
      "start": 603,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-41.png",
      "background": "field",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "1. The ground",
      "narration": "So how did a sick, hungry army win? First, the ground. The mud and the woods turned the French advantage in numbers into a traffic jam.",
      "word_count": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-42",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Why it worked",
      "start": 615,
      "duration": 6,
      "image": "images/shot-42.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "2. The longbow",
      "narration": "Second, the longbow, and the years of practice behind every single archer.",
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-43",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Why it worked",
      "start": 621,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-43.png",
      "background": "camp",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "sit"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "3. Overconfidence",
      "narration": "And third, overconfidence. The French were so sure of winning that they never really agreed on a plan. Just like Yoshimoto at Okehazama, they never imagined that the small, desperate army was the dangerous one.",
      "word_count": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-44",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 636,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-44.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Townsman",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Townsman",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "\"We few, we happy few...\"",
      "narration": "Henry returned to London a hero. Agincourt became a national legend, especially after Shakespeare wrote his play Henry the Fifth, almost two hundred years later, with its famous speech: We few, we happy few, we band of brothers.",
      "word_count": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-45",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 653,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-45.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Narrator",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Myth?",
      "narration": "There's also a popular story that a rude two-finger gesture in Britain comes from English archers, showing the French they still had their drawing fingers. It's a great story. Unfortunately, historians have found no evidence for it.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-46",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 669,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-46.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Catherine",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Treaty of Troyes, 1420",
      "narration": "Five years after Agincourt, Henry got almost everything he wanted. A treaty named him heir to the throne of France, and he married the French king's daughter, Catherine.",
      "word_count": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-47",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 681,
      "duration": 19,
      "image": "images/shot-47.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Henry V",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "1422",
      "narration": "But in 1422, Henry fell ill, probably with the same disease that had struck his army at Harfleur, and he died at just thirty-five. The French king died less than two months later. Henry missed becoming King of France by a matter of weeks.",
      "word_count": 44
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-48",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 700,
      "duration": 20,
      "image": "images/shot-48.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Farm girl",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "To be continued...",
      "narration": "His son became King of England while still a baby, and the war dragged on. And a few years later, France would find a hero in the most unlikely person imaginable: a teenage farm girl from a small village. But that's a story for another day.",
      "word_count": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "outro-1",
      "speaker": "son",
      "section": "Outro",
      "start": 720,
      "duration": 6,
      "image": "images/outro-1.png",
